# Build context exclusions.
#
# `.dockerignore` rather than relying on a pre-build `git clean`, because the
# build context is what gets sent to the daemon: a 400 MB `node_modules` that is
# excluded here never leaves the machine, and a stale one can never shadow the
# `npm ci` in the Dockerfile.

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build-test
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
.gitignore
.githooks

# Secrets. `.env.example` is kept on purpose; `.env` must never be baked into a
# layer, where it survives in the image history even if a later step deletes it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]

*.docx
~$*.docx
brand
docs
scripts
